# Kernel configuration for the opt-in "amnesia" capability (CAPS=amnesia):
# a genuinely read-only root filesystem with targeted tmpfs mounts for the
# state that must still be writable at runtime — increment #2 of the
# air-gapped GPG key-generation appliance (see package/gpg-genkey.sh).
# Design C: no overlayfs, no
# initrd — the root device is mounted ro directly (see lfs's qemu case and
# package/boot.sh's cmdline component, both cap-conditional on "amnesia" in
# $CAPS) and /var, /tmp, /root are separate tmpfs mounts laid down by
# package/amnesia-config.sh.
#
# There is nothing to turn on here: CONFIG_TMPFS[_POSIX_ACL,_XATTR]=y and
# CONFIG_BTRFS_FS=y already live in base.config (every platform's root is
# btrfs, and tmpfs is needed unconditionally for /run — this capability
# just adds more tmpfs mounts, not tmpfs support itself). This file exists
# anyway, empty of config lines, because `lfs` validates a capability's
# existence by the presence of package/linux/<cap>.config (see lfs's
# Capabilities section) — package/linux/busybox.config is the established
# precedent for a comment-only fragment kept purely for that reason.
